-- title:
--   Positive homogeneity of the cone gap
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a real inner product space, let $v \in E$, let $\vartheta \in \mathbb{R}$, let $\lambda \in \mathbb{R}$ with $\lambda \ge 0$, and let $p \in E$. With
--   $$\mathrm{gap}(v,\vartheta,p) = \langle v,p\rangle \sin\vartheta - \lVert p - \langle v,p\rangle v\rVert \cos\vartheta$$
--   the signed distance from $p$ to the boundary of the half-cone of axis $v$ and apex angle $\vartheta$, one has
--
--   $$\mathrm{gap}(v, \vartheta, \lambda p) \;=\; \lambda\, \mathrm{gap}(v,\vartheta,p).$$
--
--   So the gap is positively homogeneous of degree one in its point argument. This is the scaling law that makes the cone estimates scale-free: an estimate proved at one scale transfers verbatim to every dilate, which is what the renormalization across the geometric scales $\Delta^n$ relies on.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** No unit-length hypothesis is imposed on the axis $v$, and $\vartheta$ is an arbitrary real; only $\lambda \ge 0$ is needed, since for $\lambda < 0$ the transverse term $\lVert \lambda p - \cdots\rVert$ would pick up $|\lambda|$ rather than $\lambda$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/dbenbenn/quadratic-forms-sobolev/blob/7a1a680db2124d46ce370c91fd450aa454edf491/QuadraticFormsSobolev/ConeGap.lean#L117-L124

